[{"category":"section","location":"explanation/glossary/#Glossary","page":"Glossary","text":"Terms used throughout the docs: HNF, SNF, parent lattice, supercell, labeling, super-periodicity, orbit, stabilizer, mixed-radix hash, colex rank.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13e of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Glossary"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/select-supercells/#Select-supercells","page":"Select supercells","text":"Use VolumeRange, RadiusBound, and ExplicitHNFs to control which supercell HNFs the enumerator visits.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Select supercells"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/polya/#Pólya-counting","page":"Pólya counting","text":"Public API for the Polya submodule, including the Möbius-inversion helpers.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13b of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Pólya counting"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/super-periodicity/#Super-periodicity","page":"Super-periodicity","text":"What it means for a labeling to be fixed by a non-identity translation, why these structures are filtered by default, and when you'd keep them.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13e of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Super-periodicity"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/dispatch-and-cost-gate/#Dispatch-and-the-cost-gate","page":"Dispatch and the cost gate","text":"How enumerate picks an algorithm given the parent, sites, and supercell selection; how estimate_cost informs the gate; how to override.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13e of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Dispatch and the cost gate"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/polya-counting/#Pólya-counting","page":"Pólya counting","text":"The Pólya enumeration theorem and the Möbius-inversion correction Enumlib uses to count non-super-periodic structures without materializing them.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13e of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Pólya counting"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/count-without-enumerating/#Count-without-enumerating","page":"Count without enumerating","text":"Use count_inequivalent (Pólya/Möbius) when you want the count but not the structures.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Count without enumerating"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/handle-super-periodicity/#Handle-super-periodicity","page":"Handle super-periodicity","text":"The include_superperiodic kwarg, what it changes, and when you'd want it set to true (training-data construction) vs the default false (canonical derivative structures).\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Handle super-periodicity"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/estimate-cost/#Estimate-the-cost-of-an-enumeration","page":"Estimate the cost of an enumeration","text":"Call estimate_cost to preview operation count and memory footprint before committing to a run.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Estimate the cost of an enumeration"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/#Tutorials","page":"Tutorials","text":"Walkthroughs that teach you the package by doing real work end-to-end. Read these in order if you're new.\n\nYour first enumeration\nEnumerating at a fixed concentration\nGenerating a DFT/MLIP training database\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nTutorial content lands in Phase 13d of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This page exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Tutorials"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/write-poscars-for-dft/#Write-POSCARs-for-DFT","page":"Write POSCARs for DFT","text":"Use to_poscar and write_enumeration_archive to produce VASP-compatible POSCARs for downstream DFT or MLIP runs.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Write POSCARs for DFT"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/poscar-io/#POSCAR-I/O-and-result-attachment","page":"POSCAR I/O and result attachment","text":"Public API for to_poscar, write_enumeration_archive, read_results, and attach_results.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13b of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"POSCAR I/O and result attachment"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/#Explanation","page":"Explanation","text":"The \"why\" of Enumlib. Discussions of the underlying math, the algorithms drawn from the Hart-Forcade-Nelson papers, and the dispatch logic that picks the right one for your problem.\n\nAlgorithm overview\nExhaustive enumeration (HF 2008)\nMultinomial mixed-radix hash (HF 2012)\nRecursive stabilizer (Morgan-Hart 2017)\nPólya counting\nDispatch and the cost gate\nSuper-periodicity\nConcentration and multiplicity\nGlossary\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nExplanation content lands in Phase 13e of the v0.2 documentation rollout.","title":"Explanation"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/supercells/#Supercells-and-volume-ranges","page":"Supercells and volume ranges","text":"Public API for HNF, Supercell, VolumeRange, RadiusBound, ExplicitHNFs, and getSymInequivHNFs.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13b of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Supercells and volume ranges"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/recursive-stabilizer-2017/#Recursive-stabilizer-(Morgan-Hart-2017)","page":"Recursive stabilizer (Morgan-Hart 2017)","text":"The 2017 recursive-stabilizer tree: shrinking subgroups, partial colorings, and why it dominates at large supercell volume with many species.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13e of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Recursive stabilizer (Morgan-Hart 2017)"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/#Reference","page":"Reference","text":"Every public function, type, and keyword argument the package exposes. This quadrant is generated directly from in-source docstrings and is the authoritative description of the API surface.\n\nParent lattices and sites\nSupercells and volume ranges\nConcentrations\nenumerate and count_inequivalent\nCost estimator\nPólya counting\nPOSCAR I/O and result attachment\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nReference docstrings are audited and surfaced in Phase 13b of the v0.2 documentation rollout.","title":"Reference"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/enumerate-at-fixed-concentration/#Enumerate-at-fixed-concentration","page":"Enumerate at fixed concentration","text":"Restrict enumerate to labelings with prescribed species counts using concentration_count, Concentration (rationals), or concentration_ratio.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Enumerate at fixed concentration"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/parent-and-sites/#Parent-lattices-and-sites","page":"Parent lattices and sites","text":"Public API for ParentLattice, Site, Sites, and the equivalence helpers.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13b of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Parent lattices and sites"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/pick-an-algorithm/#Pick-an-algorithm","page":"Pick an algorithm","text":"When to set algorithm = :exhaustive, :multinomial, or :recursive — and when to leave it on the default :auto.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Pick an algorithm"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/exhaustive-2008/#Exhaustive-enumeration-(HF-2008)","page":"Exhaustive enumeration (HF 2008)","text":"How the original 2008 algorithm enumerates by visiting every coloring and quotienting by the supercell symmetry group; what it costs and where it falls down.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13e of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Exhaustive enumeration (HF 2008)"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/describe-substitution-sites/#Describe-substitution-sites","page":"Describe substitution sites","text":"Set up a Sites collection with Site entries — fractional coordinates, allowed labels per site, and how to mix substitutional and frozen positions.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Describe substitution sites"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/construct-a-parent-lattice/#Construct-a-parent-lattice","page":"Construct a parent lattice","text":"Build a ParentLattice{D} for common Bravais lattices and unconventional bases. Covers handedness, basis-vector conventions, and the two- and three-dimensional cases.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Construct a parent lattice"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/#How-to-guides","page":"How-to guides","text":"Task-oriented recipes. Each page answers a focused \"I have X, I want Y\" question without re-teaching the package fundamentals.\n\nConstruct a parent lattice\nDescribe substitution sites\nSelect supercells\nEnumerate at fixed concentration\nSweep a range of concentrations\nPick an algorithm\nCount without enumerating\nEstimate the cost of an enumeration\nHandle super-periodicity\nWrite POSCARs for DFT\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nHow-to content lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout.","title":"How-to guides"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/02-fixed-concentration/#Enumerating-at-a-fixed-concentration","page":"Enumerating at a fixed concentration","text":"Use the Concentration_* types and the concentration kwarg of enumerate to restrict the output to labelings with prescribed counts of each species.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13d of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Enumerating at a fixed concentration"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/concentrations/#Concentrations","page":"Concentrations","text":"Public API for the concentration constructors and ConcentrationRange.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13b of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Concentrations"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/cost-estimator/#Cost-estimator","page":"Cost estimator","text":"Public API for estimate_cost and the budget-gate types.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13b of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Cost estimator"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/multinomial-2012/#Multinomial-mixed-radix-hash-(HF-2012)","page":"Multinomial mixed-radix hash (HF 2012)","text":"The 2012 mixed-radix-hash extension that makes fixed-concentration enumeration tractable; the colex rank and the partition-explosion gate.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13e of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Multinomial mixed-radix hash (HF 2012)"},{"category":"section","location":"how-to/sweep-concentration-ranges/#Sweep-concentration-ranges","page":"Sweep concentration ranges","text":"Enumerate across a band of concentrations in one call using ConcentrationRange.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13c of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Sweep concentration ranges"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/algorithm-overview/#Algorithm-overview","page":"Algorithm overview","text":"A bird's-eye view of the three Hart-Forcade-Nelson enumeration algorithms, the Pólya counter, and how Enumlib chooses among them.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13e of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Algorithm overview"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/03-dft-training-database/#Generating-a-DFT/MLIP-training-database","page":"Generating a DFT/MLIP training database","text":"End-to-end workflow: enumerate → write_enumeration_archive → ship a tarball → calculator fills energy_eV= slots → read_results + attach_results → hand off to JuCE.jl. The pre-release narrative lives at docs/notes/phase11-tutorial.md and migrates here.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13d of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Generating a DFT/MLIP training database"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/concentration-and-multiplicity/#Concentration-and-multiplicity","page":"Concentration and multiplicity","text":"Why a concentration constraint constrains some supercell volumes but not others, and how the orbit-multiplicity counts relate to the unrestricted enumeration.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13e of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"Concentration and multiplicity"},{"category":"section","location":"#Enumlib.jl","page":"Home","text":"A Julia successor to the Fortran enumlib derivative-structure enumeration tool. Enumlib enumerates symmetry-inequivalent decorations of a parent crystal lattice across user-chosen supercell volumes, optionally constrained to a fixed concentration. Outputs are ready for cluster expansion fitting, DFT/MLIP training-database generation, or use as inputs to downstream materials-science workflows.\n\nThis site is organized as a Diátaxis four-quadrant documentation tree:\n\nTutorials — learn by doing. Run your first enumeration, generate a DFT training set, work end-to-end.\nHow-to guides — task-oriented recipes. \"I have X, I want Y, what calls do I make?\"\nReference — every public function, type, and kwarg. Authoritative API.\nExplanation — the why and the math. Algorithm papers, dispatch logic, super-periodicity, glossary.\n\nnote: Status\nEnumlib.jl is in active development for its v0.2.0 release. The API is settling but is not yet declared stable. See the v0.2 plan for current scope.","title":"Enumlib.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Install","page":"Home","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.develop(url = \"https://github.com/glwhart/Enumlib.jl\")  # while unregistered\nusing Enumlib\n\nAfter v0.2.0 ships to the General registry: Pkg.add(\"Enumlib\").","title":"Install"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-taste","page":"Home","text":"using Enumlib\n\nparent = ParentLattice([0.5 0.5 0.0;\n                        0.5 0.0 0.5;\n                        0.0 0.5 0.5])             # FCC primitive\nsites  = Sites([Site([0.0, 0.0, 0.0], [0, 1])])   # binary case, one site\n\nenum = enumerate(parent, sites; supercells = VolumeRange(1:4))\nlength(enum)\n\nFor more, head to the first-enumeration tutorial.","title":"Quick taste"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/enumerate-and-count/#enumerate-and-count_inequivalent","page":"enumerate and count_inequivalent","text":"Authoritative signature, kwargs, and return-type documentation for the two top-level entry points.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13b of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds end-to-end during infrastructure setup.","title":"enumerate and count_inequivalent"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/01-first-enumeration/#Your-first-enumeration","page":"Your first enumeration","text":"Build a parent lattice, declare substitution sites, and run enumerate on a small supercell range. By the end you'll have a Vector{EnumeratedStructure} to inspect.\n\nwarning: Phase 13a placeholder\nContent lands in Phase 13d (tutorials build-out) of the v0.2 documentation rollout. This stub exists so the site builds during infra setup.","title":"Your first enumeration"}]
